# vtium's capability list: NAME STATUS ISSUE ROWS NOTE, which
# `conformance probes` judges through the capability scenario that declares
# each NAME (README.md, The capability scenarios).
# works: the scenario must pass. missing: it must fail, and ISSUE is the
# vtium/vtium issue that owes the capability. A missing capability whose
# scenario starts passing fails the run until it is set to works.
# ROWS: the ADR-1000 rows the scenario judges, comma-separated, from which
# COVERAGE.md takes the tests that guard it (tools/conformance/README.md).

# text and attributes
sgr-colon-subparams           works   -     sgr.extended-color             colon sub-parameters: SGR reads them, other sequences with them are ignored
sgr-underline-styles          works   -     sgr.underline-style            SGR 4:1 to 4:5 and 21 set each underline style, 24 clears
sgr-underline-colour          works   -     sgr.underline-color            SGR 58;2, 58:2::r:g:b and 59; 4;58;5;196 never blinks
sgr-strike                    works   -     sgr.strike                     SGR 9 and 29
sgr-blink                     works   -     sgr.blink                      SGR 5 and 25 set the frame's blink flag
sgr-italic                    works   -     sgr.italic                     SGR 3 and 23
sgr-truecolor                 works   -     sgr.extended-color             SGR 38;2 and 48;2
sgr-overline                  works   -     sgr.overline                   SGR 53 and 55, which the views print as overline (attrs-renditions)
sgr-super-subscript           works   -     sgr.script                     SGR 73 to 75, which the views print as superscript and subscript (attrs-renditions)
palette-at-draw               works   -     sgr.draw-time-color            colors are resolved at draw time: a palette change recolors text
modkeys-not-sgr               works   -     input.modify-other-keys        CSI > 4;1 m and CSI ? 4 m are not SGR 4
cluster                       works   -     text.grapheme                  a grapheme cluster is one cell whose codepoints read back
mode-2027                     works   -     DEC-2027                       mode 2027 and its DECRQM reply
vs16-width                    works   -     text.vs-width                  VS16 widens U+2764 to two cells under mode 2027
wide-at-margin                works   -     text.vs-width                  a wide character wraps whole at the margin
rep                           works   -     text.rep                       REP repeats the last printed character, a wide one whole
erase-colours-only            works   -     ctl.bce                        EL, SU, SD and RI blanks take the pen background only
frame-age-per-caller          works   -     platform.multi-monitor         each frame-since caller keeps its own changes
reflow                        works   -     text.reflow                    a resize rewraps the lines a wrap made
bidi                          works   -Dbidi text.bidi                     a mixed line draws in the order the bidirectional algorithm gives

# modes and replies
mode-2026-sync                works   -     DEC-2026                       mode 2026 holds frames while the host offers it
decrqm                        works   -     query.decrqm                   DECRQM reports a mode's state
da1                           works   -     query.da1                      DA1 replies
da1-level                     works   -     query.da1                      DA1 reports a level xterm defines
da2                           works   -     query.da2                      DA2 replies
da3                           works   -     query.da3                      DA3 answers DECRPTUI
xtversion                     works   -     query.xtversion                XTVERSION replies with the host's text
xtgettcap                     works   -     query.xtgettcap                XTGETTCAP answers from vtium's table, the fixtures/kmscon.termcap fixture
osc-4-query                   works   -     color.palette.query            OSC 4 queries a palette color
osc-4-set                     works   -     color.palette.set              OSC 4 sets a palette color
osc-10-11-query               works   -     color.dynamic.query            OSC 10 and 11 query the default colors
osc-10-11-set                 works   -     color.dynamic.set              OSC 10 and 11 set the default colors
osc-12-query                  works   -     color.dynamic.set              OSC 12 queries the cursor color
osc-104-110-111-reset         works   -     color.palette.set              OSC 104, 110 and 111 reset what OSC 4, 10 and 11 set
mode-1042-bell                works   -     DEC-1042,ctl.bel               each BEL reaches the host while mode 1042 is set, none once it is reset

# input
kitty-keyboard                works   -     input.kitty-keyboard           the kitty keyboard protocol: CSI ? u reports the flags in force
modify-other-keys             works   -     input.modify-other-keys        modifyOtherKeys encodes modified keys
mouse-1000                    works   -     DEC-1000                       normal mouse tracking
mouse-1006                    works   -     DEC-1006                       SGR mouse reports
mouse-1006-first              works   -     DEC-1006                       SGR mouse reports set before tracking
mouse-1003-sgr                works   -     DEC-1003                       any-event tracking in SGR form
mouse-1003-x10                works   -     DEC-1003                       any-event tracking in the X10 form
mouse-1016                    works   -     DEC-1016                       SGR-Pixels mouse reports
bracketed-paste               works   -     DEC-2004                       a paste in mode 2004 is bracketed
focus-1004                    works   -     DEC-1004                       focus in and out reported in mode 1004
select-copy                   works   -     clipboard.selection            a word, a line and a drag selected and copied, and a copy with nothing selected
key-backspace-del             works   -     input.legacy                   BackSpace sends BS, then DEL once the host chooses it
key-kitty-events              missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 2: a press, a repeat and a release, and no release once the flags are 0 (needs key-events)
key-kitty-events-legacy-keys  missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 2: Enter, Tab and BackSpace keep their bytes and send no release, nor does a text key (needs key-events)
key-kitty-shifted-key         missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 4: a key held with Shift sends its shifted key
key-kitty-unshifted-key       missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           the key code is the unshifted key the host reports, or the symbol when it reports none (needs key-forms)
key-kitty-base-layout-key     missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 4: Ctrl+С on a Russian layout sends the base layout key c (needs key-forms)
key-kitty-all-keys            missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 8: text keys, Enter, Tab, BackSpace and a modifier key send escape codes, and RIS ends it
key-kitty-all-keys-events     missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flags 2 and 8: a text key, Enter and Shift report their releases (needs key-events)
key-kitty-associated-text     missing #42   input.kitty-keyboard           flag 16: a key sends its text in the escape code, and never a control character

# strings vtium does not take yet
osc-8-hyperlink               missing #40   osc.8                          a placeholder scenario: OSC 8 hyperlinks
osc-52-clipboard              works   -     osc.52.write                   OSC 52 sets the clipboard, which the host takes once
osc-133-marks                 works   -     osc.133                        the view jumps between the prompts OSC 133 marks, and a command's output selects whole

# images: working in a build with images and failing, as a missing capability
# must, in one without. The list names the build feature -Dimages; vtium's
# is vtium-image (sixel #48, kitty graphics #49), which vtium-replay is
# built with.
sixel                         works   -Dimages image.sixel,query.xtsmgraphics DA1 attribute 4, and XTSMGRAPHICS reads the register count (#48)
kitty-graphics                works   -Dimages image.kitty                  a kitty a=q with an id gets OK (#49)
mode-80                       works   -Dimages DEC-80                       DECRQM 80 (DECSDM) replies 1 or 2 while sixel is on (#48)
mode-1070                     works   -Dimages DEC-1070                     DECRQM 1070 (private sixel registers) replies 1 or 2 (#48)
mode-8452                     works   -Dimages DEC-8452                     DECRQM 8452 (sixel cursor right) replies 1 or 2 (#48)

# the modes and controls the copied capability scenarios do not cover (#54);
# 1007, 1035 and XTSHIFTESCAPE need host calls the interface has no command
# for
decaln                        works   -     ctl.decaln                     ESC # 8 fills the screen with E, origin mode off, the margins the whole screen
state-margins-tabs            works   -     ctl.decstbm,ctl.tabs           the state lines show the scroll region, the left and right margins and the tab stops
reverse-wrap                  works   -     DEC-45                         mode 45: BS reverse-wraps only into the row that wrapped
xtsave                        works   -     ctl.xtsave                     XTSAVE and XTRESTORE of one mode, and the empty list, which leaves DECOM
decslrm                       works   -     DEC-69,ctl.decslrm             mode 69 makes CSI s set left and right margins, text wraps and scrolls inside them, DECRQSS reports them
decic                         works   -     ctl.decic                      DECIC, DECDC and DECBI move the columns between the margins
mouse-1015                    works   -     DEC-1015                       mode 1015: the urxvt mouse encoding
decnkm                        works   -     DEC-66                         mode 66: the keypad's application mode, which DECKPNM resets
meta-keys                     works   -     DEC-1034,DEC-1036              modes 1036 and 1034: ESC before an Alt key, or its eighth bit
